1
00:01:05,627 --> 00:01:08,714
<i>America is an irradiated wasteland.</i>

2
00:01:10,465 --> 00:01:12,426
<i>Within it lies a city.</i>

3
00:01:14,386 --> 00:01:17,514
<i>Outside the boundary walls a desert.</i>

4
00:01:17,598 --> 00:01:19,308
<i>A cursed earth.</i>

5
00:01:20,809 --> 00:01:24,313
<i>Inside the walls a cursed city,</i>

6
00:01:24,396 --> 00:01:27,774
<i>stretching from Boston to Washington, D.C.</i>

7
00:01:28,901 --> 00:01:31,570
<i>An unbroken concrete landscape.</i>

8
00:01:33,322 --> 00:01:34,740
<i>800 million people</i>

9
00:01:34,823 --> 00:01:37,784
<i>living in the ruin of the old world</i>

10
00:01:38,452 --> 00:01:41,121
<i>and the mega structures of the new one.</i>

11
00:01:43,415 --> 00:01:46,752
<i>Mega blocks. Mega highways.</i>

12
00:01:48,170 --> 00:01:50,088
<i>Mega City One.</i>

13
00:01:58,847 --> 00:02:01,934
<i>Convulsing. Choking.</i>

14
00:02:04,519 --> 00:02:06,980
<i>Breaking under its own weight.</i>

15
00:02:11,109 --> 00:02:13,779
<i>Citizens in fear of the street.</i>

16
00:02:14,321 --> 00:02:17,991
<i>The gun. The gang.</i>

17
00:02:22,371 --> 00:02:25,707
<i>Only one thing fighting
for order in the chaos,</i>

18
00:02:26,959 --> 00:02:29,795
<i>the men and women of the Hall of Justice.</i>

19
00:02:34,049 --> 00:02:35,467
<i>Juries.</i>

20
00:02:37,636 --> 00:02:39,179
<i>Executioners.</i>

21
00:02:41,890 --> 00:02:43,016
<i>Judges.</i>

22
00:02:52,317 --> 00:02:55,654
<i>Responders needed
at a square at 1117.</i>

23
00:02:55,737 --> 00:02:56,822
<i>Code 10-10.</i>

24
00:02:56,905 --> 00:02:57,990
<i>Leisure complex.</i>

25
00:02:58,073 --> 00:02:59,116
<i>Shots fired.</i>

26
00:02:59,199 --> 00:03:00,575
<i>Out of vehicle, in pursuit.</i>

27
00:03:00,659 --> 00:03:02,119
<i>Request aerial surveillance.</i>

28
00:03:02,202 --> 00:03:03,245
<i>I have a control drone</i>

29
00:03:03,328 --> 00:03:05,414
flagging three perps.

30
00:03:05,831 --> 00:03:08,834
Responders needed
in Sub-Sector 20, Flyover 5.

31
00:03:08,917 --> 00:03:11,253
We have a positive ID on three suspects

32
00:03:11,336 --> 00:03:12,504
wanted on multiple counts.

33
00:03:12,587 --> 00:03:14,172
Any Judges, please respond.

34
00:03:15,924 --> 00:03:20,429
Dredd to Control.
In pursuit of vehicle, Sector 13.

35
00:03:22,264 --> 00:03:23,348
Driving erratic.

36
00:03:23,432 --> 00:03:26,268
Suspects are under the
influence of narcotics.

37
00:03:49,458 --> 00:03:53,628
Got a Judge on our tail.

38
00:03:55,297 --> 00:03:56,298
What?

39
00:03:56,465 --> 00:03:58,216
I said, we got a Judge on our tail!

40
00:03:58,300 --> 00:04:00,635
Take him out or we're dead fucking meat!

41
00:04:03,263 --> 00:04:04,306
Fuck!

42
00:04:05,974 --> 00:04:07,309
Do you require backup?

43
00:04:07,601 --> 00:04:08,602
No.

44
00:04:11,813 --> 00:04:13,315
Fucker!

45
00:04:18,820 --> 00:04:21,323
I can't get him! Straighten the fuck out!

46
00:04:35,670 --> 00:04:36,755
<i>Be advised.</i>

47
00:04:36,838 --> 00:04:37,923
<i>We have lost visual.</i>

48
00:04:43,303 --> 00:04:45,472
Fuck, he's right on us!

49
00:04:45,972 --> 00:04:49,142
Oh, man, we're dead. We're fucking dead!

50
00:05:00,779 --> 00:05:03,115
Control. Perps just wiped out an innocent.

51
00:05:03,198 --> 00:05:05,117
I'm taking them down.

52
00:05:24,553 --> 00:05:26,680
Bike. Activate crowd control.

53
00:05:26,805 --> 00:05:29,391
<i>Activated.
Citizens, be calm.</i>

54
00:05:29,474 --> 00:05:31,309
<i>Step back from the crime scene.</i>

55
00:05:31,393 --> 00:05:35,147
<i>Interference carries
an automatic five-year sentence</i>

56
00:05:35,230 --> 00:05:36,398
<i>in the iso-cubes.</i>

57
00:05:46,700 --> 00:05:48,743
Hey, fucking get out of here!

58
00:06:08,930 --> 00:06:11,516
Control. Paramedics to my GPS.

59
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:13,602
Multiple wounded and bodies for Resyk.

60
00:06:13,935 --> 00:06:15,604
<i>Copy, Dredd.</i>

61
00:06:17,272 --> 00:06:18,523
<i>All shoppers are reminded</i>

62
00:06:18,607 --> 00:06:21,443
<i>to avoid the level 1 food courts
until further notice.</i>

63
00:06:21,568 --> 00:06:23,361
<i>Alternative refreshments can be found...</i>

64
00:06:23,445 --> 00:06:25,530
Shut the fuck up.

65
00:06:43,298 --> 00:06:46,218
- Let's talk.
- Talk about what, Judge?

66
00:06:47,802 --> 00:06:50,222
Release the hostage unharmed,

67
00:06:50,305 --> 00:06:52,224
and I guarantee you a sentence of life

68
00:06:52,307 --> 00:06:54,976
in an iso-cube without parole.

69
00:06:55,477 --> 00:06:56,978
Life without parole?

70
00:06:57,103 --> 00:06:58,383
That's the deal you're offering?

71
00:06:58,396 --> 00:07:00,148
Only if you comply.

72
00:07:00,649 --> 00:07:02,984
Your crimes include multiple homicide

73
00:07:03,068 --> 00:07:05,487
and the attempted murder of a judge.

74
00:07:05,654 --> 00:07:09,491
If you do not comply,
the sentence is death.

75
00:07:09,824 --> 00:07:11,993
You aren't a very good negotiator, Judge.

76
00:07:12,077 --> 00:07:14,329
You know why?
You got no fucking leverage!

77
00:07:14,412 --> 00:07:16,248
- Here's the deal.

78
00:07:16,331 --> 00:07:19,125
You let me walk or I blow
her fucking brains out. Okay?

79
00:07:22,128 --> 00:07:23,797
Negotiation's over.

80
00:07:23,922 --> 00:07:25,340
What are you doing?

81
00:07:25,423 --> 00:07:27,343
Didn't you hear what I said?
I'll kill the bitch!

82
00:07:28,301 --> 00:07:30,095
Yeah, I heard you, hotshot.

83
00:07:30,178 --> 00:07:31,179
What?

84
00:07:31,263 --> 00:07:33,265
I said "hotshot."

85
00:07:57,497 --> 00:07:59,499
<i>Control to Dredd. Come in.</i>

86
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:02,877
<i>- Is your pursuit resolved?</i>
- Affirmative.

87
00:08:02,961 --> 00:08:04,629
<i>Report back to the Hall of Justice.</i>

88
00:08:04,713 --> 00:08:06,673
<i>The Chief Judge wants to see you.</i>

89
00:08:10,051 --> 00:08:11,678
Thank you, Judge.

90
00:08:12,971 --> 00:08:14,139
<i>The level 1 food court</i>

91
00:08:14,222 --> 00:08:17,267
<i>will reopen in 30 minutes.
Thank you for your patience.</i>

92
00:08:32,657 --> 00:08:34,993
<i>Cassandra Anderson.
Twenty-one.</i>

93
00:08:35,702 --> 00:08:39,414
<i>Born in a block 100 meters
from the radiation boundary wall.</i>

94
00:08:39,539 --> 00:08:41,333
<i>At age seven, she lost both parents</i>

95
00:08:41,416 --> 00:08:43,626
<i>to residual-fallout cancer.</i>

96
00:08:43,710 --> 00:08:45,170
<i>As is usual with orphans,</i>

97
00:08:45,253 --> 00:08:48,506
she was given a Judge aptitude test
at age nine.

98
00:08:48,590 --> 00:08:50,508
It classified her as unsuitable,

99
00:08:50,592 --> 00:08:52,177
but she was entered into the Academy

100
00:08:52,260 --> 00:08:53,928
on special instruction.

101
00:08:54,929 --> 00:08:57,891
In the Academy, her record was never
better than borderline.

102
00:08:58,016 --> 00:08:59,476
Her final Academy score

103
00:08:59,559 --> 00:09:02,062
put her three percentile
points below a pass.

104
00:09:02,145 --> 00:09:03,938
So what's she doing in a uniform?

105
00:09:09,903 --> 00:09:11,654
<i>- Rookie Anderson.</i>
- Sir.

106
00:09:11,780 --> 00:09:13,656
<i>How many people are observing you?</i>

107
00:09:17,077 --> 00:09:18,203
Two.

108
00:09:18,620 --> 00:09:21,289
What can you tell me
about the person I'm with?

109
00:09:22,624 --> 00:09:25,627
Male. Another Judge.

110
00:09:27,629 --> 00:09:32,675
<i>I can feel anger. And control. But</i>

111
00:09:34,302 --> 00:09:35,970
there's something else.

112
00:09:36,304 --> 00:09:39,808
<i>Something behind the control. Something</i>

113
00:09:41,309 --> 00:09:43,770
almost...
- Okay, Anderson.

114
00:09:44,479 --> 00:09:45,814
<i>That Will do.</i>

115
00:09:46,481 --> 00:09:47,982
She's a mutant.

116
00:09:48,608 --> 00:09:51,152
The Judges Council have chosen
to overlook her status.

117
00:09:51,486 --> 00:09:52,654
So you will, too.

118
00:09:53,405 --> 00:09:55,115
She's the most powerful psychic

119
00:09:55,198 --> 00:09:57,409
we've ever come across by a huge margin.

120
00:09:58,159 --> 00:10:00,662
The Judges are losing the war for the city.

121
00:10:00,745 --> 00:10:02,664
We believe she could be a major asset.

122
00:10:03,331 --> 00:10:06,626
As I said, her final score
was only three points below a pass.

123
00:10:06,709 --> 00:10:07,919
It's marginal.

124
00:10:08,002 --> 00:10:10,046
It's not marginal. She failed.

125
00:10:10,130 --> 00:10:11,923
The girl's getting one more chance.

126
00:10:13,633 --> 00:10:16,428
I want you to take her out,
give her one day in the field.

127
00:10:16,511 --> 00:10:17,846
Supervised.

128
00:10:18,138 --> 00:10:19,681
See if she makes the grade.

129
00:10:20,432 --> 00:10:23,643
Sink or swim. Chuck her in the deep end.

130
00:10:26,104 --> 00:10:27,939
It's all the deep end.

131
00:10:29,774 --> 00:10:31,109
<i>Personnel are required</i>

132
00:10:31,192 --> 00:10:32,819
<i>to carry identification at all times.</i>

133
00:10:32,944 --> 00:10:34,112
A rookie judge on assessment

134
00:10:34,195 --> 00:10:36,030
is likely to be involved in armed combat.

135
00:10:36,114 --> 00:10:38,032
One in five don't survive the first day.

136
00:10:38,199 --> 00:10:39,909
You may be required to carry out

137
00:10:39,993 --> 00:10:41,786
on-the-spot executions of convicted felons.

138
00:10:41,870 --> 00:10:42,912
Yes, sir.

139
00:10:42,996 --> 00:10:45,874
Incorrect sentencing is an automatic fail.

140
00:10:45,957 --> 00:10:48,376
Disobeying a direct order
from your assessment officer

141
00:10:48,460 --> 00:10:50,128
is an automatic fail.

142
00:10:50,545 --> 00:10:54,340
Losing your primary weapon or having it
taken from you is an automatic fail.

143
00:10:54,424 --> 00:10:55,467
Yes, sir.

144
00:10:55,550 --> 00:10:57,218
Are you ready, rookie?

145
00:10:57,302 --> 00:10:58,720
I am.

146
00:10:58,887 --> 00:11:00,638
<i>Mandatory vehicle checks...</i>

147
00:11:00,722 --> 00:11:02,140
Your assessment starts now.

148
00:12:28,726 --> 00:12:29,978
Ma.

149
00:12:39,571 --> 00:12:41,239
We got trouble.

150
00:12:46,494 --> 00:12:49,831
They were selling Sternhammer product
on my level.

151
00:12:50,248 --> 00:12:52,584
I warned them off with a beating
a couple of weeks ago.

152
00:12:52,667 --> 00:12:53,835
Guess it didn't work.

153
00:12:54,127 --> 00:12:55,670
You can't deal with it yourself?

154
00:12:56,129 --> 00:12:57,630
I can deal with it.

155
00:12:57,922 --> 00:13:00,203
The question is whether you
wanna make an example of them.

156
00:13:04,345 --> 00:13:07,473
Skin them. Toss them over the balcony.

157
00:13:08,016 --> 00:13:09,892
Hit them with a little slo-mo first?

158
00:13:11,311 --> 00:13:12,353
Sure.

159
00:13:19,694 --> 00:13:21,112
- Eat this, fucker!

160
00:13:21,529 --> 00:13:22,864
Hold him down!

161
00:13:23,823 --> 00:13:25,825
Please. Oh, please.

162
00:14:09,869 --> 00:14:11,996
<i>Responders in
the vicinity of Peach Trees.</i>

163
00:14:12,080 --> 00:14:14,123
<i>We have a report of a triple homicide.</i>

164
00:14:14,207 --> 00:14:17,960
<i>The paramedic is on site
and is cordoning off the area.</i>

165
00:14:25,885 --> 00:14:28,680
12 serious crimes
reported every minute.

166
00:14:28,763 --> 00:14:30,181
17,000 per day.

167
00:14:30,765 --> 00:14:32,684
We can respond to around 6%.

168
00:14:32,767 --> 00:14:33,768
Which 6%?

169
00:14:34,602 --> 00:14:36,771
Your show, rookie.
You tell me.

170
00:14:38,398 --> 00:14:40,400
Peach Trees.
Multiple homicide.

171
00:14:40,608 --> 00:14:42,777
Dredd to Control.
We'll take Peach Trees.

172
00:14:43,277 --> 00:14:44,737
<i>Copy that.</i>

173
00:15:08,094 --> 00:15:10,054
Hey, Joey,
show us what you've got.

174
00:15:15,101 --> 00:15:16,144
Okay, rookie.

175
00:15:16,227 --> 00:15:17,812
What do you know
about Peach Trees?

176
00:15:17,895 --> 00:15:21,107
Sir. Peach Trees houses
75,000 registered citizens.

177
00:15:21,190 --> 00:15:23,234
It has the highest
crime rate in Sector 13.

178
00:15:23,317 --> 00:15:25,361
Unemployment rate of 96%.

179
00:15:25,445 --> 00:15:27,286
And more than half the
residential levels here

180
00:15:27,321 --> 00:15:28,614
are classed as slums.

181
00:15:32,618 --> 00:15:33,745
Rookie.

182
00:15:35,246 --> 00:15:36,247
Judgment.

183
00:15:36,330 --> 00:15:38,249
Vagrancy, three weeks, iso-cubes.

184
00:15:38,332 --> 00:15:39,751
But prioritize murders?

185
00:15:39,834 --> 00:15:42,670
Correct. Don't be here when we get back.

186
00:15:42,754 --> 00:15:44,380
Yes. Thanks, Judge.

187
00:15:46,340 --> 00:15:49,010
<i>Please remain behind the security tape.</i>

188
00:15:50,094 --> 00:15:52,096
So why do you wanna be a judge?

189
00:15:52,180 --> 00:15:54,891
Sir. I want to protect and serve the city.

190
00:15:54,974 --> 00:15:56,434
To make a difference.

191
00:15:56,517 --> 00:15:58,686
Make a difference to a block like this?

192
00:15:59,312 --> 00:16:01,189
It's yours if you want it.

193
00:16:01,564 --> 00:16:03,691
I was born and raised in a block like this

194
00:16:03,775 --> 00:16:05,735
before the Justice Department took me.

195
00:16:05,818 --> 00:16:07,779
I know there are good people inside,

196
00:16:07,862 --> 00:16:10,823
good families just trying to get by.

197
00:16:12,283 --> 00:16:14,577
Yes, I believe I can make a difference.

198
00:16:16,704 --> 00:16:18,039
Admirable.

199
00:16:19,332 --> 00:16:21,292
<i>The mall will be closing today at 10:00.</i>

200
00:16:21,375 --> 00:16:23,419
<i>Plenty of time
to make your purchases.</i>

201
00:16:26,339 --> 00:16:27,381
What have you got?

202
00:16:27,465 --> 00:16:30,384
Three stiffs
in a somewhat fucked-up condition.

203
00:16:31,344 --> 00:16:33,638
Oh, did you get a picture of that?

204
00:16:33,721 --> 00:16:34,972
You based in Peach Trees?

205
00:16:35,056 --> 00:16:36,849
Med Center, level 25.

206
00:16:36,974 --> 00:16:38,601
- You ID'd them?
- Mostly.

207
00:16:38,684 --> 00:16:40,311
These two are registered to this block.

208
00:16:40,394 --> 00:16:41,437
And him?

209
00:16:41,521 --> 00:16:43,815
I'll have to run his blood
through a DNA profiler.

210
00:16:43,898 --> 00:16:45,900
If I can figure out which blood is his.

211
00:16:52,907 --> 00:16:54,228
What do you make of this, rookie?

212
00:16:56,369 --> 00:16:57,578
I don't know, sir.

213
00:17:03,167 --> 00:17:05,169
It's a cold-burn from a slo-mo inhaler.

214
00:17:05,837 --> 00:17:06,963
Slo-mo?

215
00:17:07,380 --> 00:17:10,633
Only just hit the grid,
but it's making big waves.

216
00:17:10,716 --> 00:17:11,926
Makes the brain feel as if

217
00:17:12,009 --> 00:17:14,512
time is passing at 1% its normal speed.

218
00:17:16,264 --> 00:17:18,516
Guess it felt like a long way down.

219
00:17:32,905 --> 00:17:34,490
Positive on your IDs.

220
00:17:34,991 --> 00:17:37,702
All showing convictions for
possession of narcotics.

221
00:17:38,411 --> 00:17:39,537
Transmitting data now.

222
00:17:41,414 --> 00:17:44,458
Small-time perps. Junkies.
No known gang affiliation.

223
00:17:44,542 --> 00:17:45,793
What's your analysis?

224
00:17:47,753 --> 00:17:50,131
Drugged. Skinned.
Displayed in public.

225
00:17:50,631 --> 00:17:52,550
I think it's a punishment killing.

226
00:17:52,633 --> 00:17:54,552
Someone's trying to send a message.

227
00:17:54,635 --> 00:17:57,805
Yeah. Don't fuck with the Ma-Ma Clan.

228
00:17:59,307 --> 00:18:00,641
Ma-Ma Clan?

229
00:18:04,645 --> 00:18:07,398
We have her
on record from her whoring days.

230
00:18:07,481 --> 00:18:09,358
The picture's pretty old

231
00:18:09,442 --> 00:18:13,988
but that's her.
Madeline Madrigal, aka Ma-Ma.

232
00:18:14,655 --> 00:18:17,199
Ex-hooker from the S-9 pleasure district.

233
00:18:17,992 --> 00:18:20,494
Quit working when she got
sliced up by her pimp.

234
00:18:20,786 --> 00:18:22,163
She got her own back.

235
00:18:22,622 --> 00:18:25,249
Block legend says
she feminized the guy with her teeth.

236
00:18:26,167 --> 00:18:29,670
Took over his business interests
and never looked back.

237
00:18:30,421 --> 00:18:32,673
Anyone else, you'd say
it was bullshit, right?

238
00:18:33,674 --> 00:18:36,844
<i>Not with Ma-Ma.
Her trademark is violence.</i>

239
00:18:41,140 --> 00:18:43,768
<i>Not so long ago
there were three main gangs</i>

240
00:18:43,851 --> 00:18:46,020
<i>hustling for control of Peach Trees.</i>

241
00:18:46,646 --> 00:18:50,358
The Peyote Kings,
the Red Dragons, the Judged.

242
00:18:51,150 --> 00:18:52,526
<i>Then Ma-Ma arrived.</i>

243
00:18:58,991 --> 00:19:00,034
What the fuck?

244
00:19:02,036 --> 00:19:03,287
Let's go!

245
00:19:04,956 --> 00:19:06,557
<i>Took over the top floor of the block</i>

246
00:19:06,624 --> 00:19:08,376
<i>and started working her way down.</i>

247
00:19:10,211 --> 00:19:13,547
Nine months later,
she had control of everything.

248
00:19:13,714 --> 00:19:15,967
Levels 1 to 200

249
00:19:16,801 --> 00:19:18,135
<i>are hers.</i>

250
00:19:19,053 --> 00:19:20,388
How did she get away with it?

251
00:19:20,471 --> 00:19:23,724
You know how often we get
a judge up in Peach Trees?

252
00:19:24,642 --> 00:19:26,268
Well, you got one now.

253
00:19:27,561 --> 00:19:31,065
The victims are registered
to apartments on level 39.

254
00:19:31,399 --> 00:19:33,109
Likely killed over a turf issue,

255
00:19:33,359 --> 00:19:35,319
so perps will be in the vicinity.

256
00:19:37,071 --> 00:19:38,364
Rookie.

257
00:19:38,864 --> 00:19:42,076
Find out where the Clan
operate on this level, and hit it hard.

258
00:19:45,830 --> 00:19:47,248
That would be here.

259
00:20:56,484 --> 00:20:58,736
Take it this is
your first time in non-sim combat.

260
00:20:58,819 --> 00:21:00,237
Yes, sir.

261
00:21:00,321 --> 00:21:01,989
Been wondering when you'd remember

262
